alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The idna_oracle entry, invoked as `idna_oracle PATH` with PATH naming the case file that tests/text/idna_oracle.py writes, relative to the working directory: per case, one line holding the domain's values as lowercase hexadecimal numbers separated by single spaces, and an empty line for the empty domain. Every value up to 0xFFFFFFFF is passed to domain_to_ascii as it is, a value that is not a Unicode scalar value included. For every case it runs domain_to_ascii with an output that already holds a nonempty sentinel prefix and prints one line: the bytes appended after the prefix as a JSON string, with quotation marks, reverse solidi and bytes below 0x20 escaped, or `null` when domain_to_ascii refuses the case with Invalid. The line is instead the JSON string `\"driver: prefix damaged\"` when the prefix is not intact after the call, `\"driver: output changed on refusal\"` when a refusal leaves bytes after the prefix, `\"driver: non-ASCII output\"` when an appended byte is 0x80 or above, `\"driver: too large\"` when domain_to_ascii refuses the case with TooLarge, and `\"driver: case too large\"` for a case of more than 16777216 values. It exits with 0 after printing every case, and with 2, after the cases before it, when the argument is missing, the case file cannot be read or it is malformed: a token that is not a lowercase hexadecimal number up to 0xFFFFFFFF, an empty token or a last line without a line feed.";
